# 2026-07-17 17:20:13.816158
+Ορίστε ένα έτοιμο prompt στα αγγλικά που μπορείς να το δώσεις σε εργαλείο σαν το Claude Code για να διορθώσει το πρόβλημα και να φτιάξει καινούριο README:
+I have a Flask-based "Emotion Detector" web app (multilingual sentiment/emotion 
+analysis). The backend server (server.py) runs fine locally — logs confirm 
+POST /analyze requests return 200 OK — but the frontend UI shows a 
+"Connection error" / "Couldn't reach the server" message when I click 
+"Analyze Emotion".
+
+Please investigate and fix the disconnect between frontend and backend. 
+Specifically check:
+
+1. The fetch/XHR call in the frontend (likely inside the `templates` folder) — 
+   verify it's pointing to the correct URL/port (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:5000/analyze) 
+   and not a stale/incorrect endpoint (such as a leftover cloud_function URL).
+2. Whether CORS headers are properly configured in server.py if frontend and 
+   backend are served from different origins/ports.
+3. Whether there's a mismatch between how the server is being run (host/port, 
+   0.0.0.0 vs 127.0.0.1) and what the frontend expects.
+4. Any mixed content issues (https frontend calling http backend).
+5. Error handling in the frontend JS so that connection errors show more 
+   specific diagnostic info (status code, actual error message) instead of 
+   a generic message.
+
+Please review the project structure:
+- cloud_function/
+- EmotionDetection/
+- templates/
+- __init__.py
+- _smoke.py
+- _where.py
+- app.yaml
+- README.md
+- requirements.txt
+- server.py
+
+Fix the root cause so the "Analyze Emotion" button reliably reaches the 
+backend and displays results.
+
+After fixing the bug, please also rewrite README.md from scratch to be 
+clean, accurate, and well-formatted. It should include:
+- A short project description/overview
+- Key features (multilingual support, sentiment/emotion analysis, etc.)
+- Project structure overview
+- Setup/installation instructions (dependencies from requirements.txt)
+- How to run the server locally
+- How to use the web UI
+- API endpoint documentation (e.g. POST /analyze — request/response format)
+- Troubleshooting section (including the connection error issue we just fixed)
+- Tech stack used
+
+Make the README visually clean using proper Markdown formatting (headers, 
+code blocks, tables where useful, and maybe badges if appropriate).

